const we4T = table(['Step', 'Working'], [['Slope of the given line', r`$\dfrac{5 - (-3)}{2 - (-1)} = \dfrac{8}{3}$`], ['Parallel line has the same slope', r`$m = \dfrac{8}{3}$`], ['Point-slope form through $(4, 1)$', r`$y - 1 = \dfrac{8}{3}(x - 4)$`], ['Clear the fraction', `$3y - 3 = 8x - 32$, so $${eqTex(w4L)}$`]], 'Table: the line through minus 1, minus 3 and 2, 5 has slope eight thirds; the parallel line through 4, 1 is y minus 1 equals eight thirds times x minus 4, which is 8x minus 3y minus 29 equals 0.', 'A parallel line keeps the slope; only the point changes.');

